WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.663
First: Microsoft's role runs in check
mode on a host without the agent.

3
00:00:06.663 --> 00:00:07.674
What happens?

4
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.762
The answer is b: it fails
at Get azcmagent status,

5
00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:15.275
and with the version check skipped,
it decides the agent is installed.

6
00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:19.408
That's why the kit's playbook doesn't call
the role at all without the confirm flag,

7
00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:21.788
and prints what each
server would get instead.

8
00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:25.338
Second: the wave zero plan
finds a production server.

9
00:00:25.338 --> 00:00:26.349
What happens?

10
00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:30.355
The answer is b: the plan stops,
and no server is contacted,

11
00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:33.925
because waves zero and one
are for non-production.

12
00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:36.088
You saw that in step six of the lab.

13
00:00:36.088 --> 00:00:41.133
The module page has two more questions, on
the owner typo and on the confirm flag,

14
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.920
each linked to the
section that answers it.
